drm/vc4: make the fbdev emulation 32 bits per pixel, red first

Faraday's own change, not from mainline.

vc4 sets up the kernel's generic fbdev emulation at RGB565, and at 32
bits that emulation picks XRGB8888, blue first in memory. The shell's
frame is RGBA, red first. At 16 bits the shell converted every pixel to
RGB565 on the CPU; at XRGB8888 it would still exchange red and blue. The
planes read XBGR8888 as it is (vc4_plane.c lists it among the HVS
formats), so with that format the shell copies its frame to the
framebuffer as it is.

- vc4 asks for an XBGR8888 fbdev (drm_client_setup_with_fourcc).
- The generic DMA fbdev picks XBGR8888 where the legacy table gives
  XRGB8888. The fbdev client keeps only the colour mode (32) of the
  fourcc it is given, so the format cannot be told here from what vc4
  asked for.
- drm_fb_helper_fill_pixel_fmt reports red at bit 0 and blue at bit 16
  for XBGR8888, so the console and the boot logo keep their colours.

The second and third changes reach every driver that uses the generic
DMA fbdev emulation; vc4 is the only DRM driver this board builds. The
second changes XRGB8888 to XBGR8888 for any such driver, with no effect
today.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c
@@ -1172,6 +1172,11 @@
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
+
+	if (format->format == DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888) {
+		var->red.offset = 0;
+		var->blue.offset = 16;
+	}
 }
 
 static void __fill_var(struct fb_var_screeninfo *var, struct fb_info *info,
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fbdev_dma.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fbdev_dma.c
@@ -285,6 +285,9 @@
 
 	format = drm_driver_legacy_fb_format(dev, sizes->surface_bpp,
 					     sizes->surface_depth);
+	/* Red first in memory, which is the order the planes read. */
+	if (format == DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888)
+		format = DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888;
 	buffer = drm_client_framebuffer_create(client, sizes->surface_width,
 					       sizes->surface_height, format);
 	if (IS_ERR(buffer))
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
@@ -432,7 +432,7 @@
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err;
 
-	drm_client_setup_with_fourcc(drm, DRM_FORMAT_RGB565);
+	drm_client_setup_with_fourcc(drm, DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888);
 
 	return 0;
 
